[FEN "r1b2bk1/1pq3pp/p2pp3/4n1PB/3QP3/2N1B3/PPP4P/5RK1 w - - 0 18"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1b2bk1/1pq3pp/p2pp3/4n1PB/3QP3/2N1B3/PPP4P/5RK1_w_-_-_0_18"]

{ He wants to bring his bishop out by d7 and c6, and then he would be fine. }
18. Nd5 { The knight lands on d5. If his e pawn takes, your queen takes back with check. If his bishop goes to d7, the knight forks from b6. [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd5b6,Gd5g8] } (18. Bf4 { A natural move, but his bishop gets out to d7. } 18... Bd7 19. Qf2 Be8 { His bishop is free, and the game is level. [%csl Gd7] }) (18. Na4 { The knight goes to the rim and gets kicked. } 18... b5 19. Nb6 Rb8 20. Nxc8 Rxc8 { Your knight traded itself for his bishop, and the game is level. }) (18. h4 { A pawn move, and his bishop gets out anyway. } 18... Bd7 19. Qd2 Be8 { His bishop is out on e8, and he is slightly better. }) (18. Qd2 { The queen steps back, and the bishop comes out regardless. } 18... Bd7 19. Bd4 g6 { His bishop reached d7, and it is about level. }) 18... Qc6 { His queen steps to c6 and hits your knight. Where does it go? } 19. Nb6 { The knight goes to b6 and attacks his rook on a8, and his bishop on c8 still cannot come out. [%csl Gb6,Rc8][%tail] } (19. Nb4 { The queen comes back, and you go round in circles. } 19... Qc7 20. Nd5 Qc6 { Back where you both started, and nothing gained. }) (19. Qb6 { You offer the queens, and he takes the trade. } 19... Bd7 20. Qxc6 Bxc6 { The queens are off and his bishop got out to c6. Level. [%csl Gc6] }) (19. Rxf8+ { This trade gives up your f column. } 19... Kxf8 20. Nb6 Rb8 { You gave a rook for his bishop, and it is level. }) (19. Nc3 { Back home, and his bishop comes straight out. } 19... Bd7 20. Be2 b5 { His bishop is free, and he is a little better. }) 19... Rb8 20. Bf4 { His rook had to leave a8, and his bishop is still at home on c8. Your bishop on f4 now presses on d6 too. [%csl Rc8,Gb6][%cal Gf4d6] } 1-0


[Event "Strategy: the weak colour, lesson"]
