{ He has no light bishop left. His rook on c6 stands in front of your c pawn. }
20... R6c7 { His rook steps back to c7. What is your best move? } 21. Be5 { Bishop to e5 hits the rook on c7 and gains a move. It also clears d4 for your queen. [%cal Ge5c7][%csl Gd4] } (21. Qb3 { The queen guards b5, but he pushes a5 and the pawns lock. [%csl Gb5] } 21... a5 22. Be5 axb4 23. Bxc7 Qxc7 { You won the exchange for a pawn, but the queen side is locked. Still better. [%csl Rb4] }) (21. a5 { Also good, but the rook is never chased. } 21... Ne8 22. Be5 Bd6 { A little slower, and you are still better. }) (21. Qc2 { A quiet move, and he gets a5 in first. } 21... a5 22. Bb5 Qd8 { Your queen side pawns are frozen, and it is level. [%csl Ra5] }) (21. b5 { Too soon: the break comes before the bishop reaches e5. } 21... axb5 22. Be5 Rxc5 { Your c pawn is gone, and he is a little better. [%csl Rc5] }) (21. Bxf6 { You trade your good bishop for his knight. } 21... Bxf6 22. a5 g6 { His bishop on f6 is happy, and your edge is small. [%csl Gf6] }) (21. Rb1 { Slow, and he gets a5 in anyway. } 21... a5 22. Be5 axb4 { He won a pawn on b4. You are a pawn down, but still slightly better. }) 21... Rc6 { The rook goes back to c6. How do you grab the light squares for good? } 22. a5 { Pawn to a5: b6 is yours now, his b pawn on b7 is stuck, and his bishop has no light squares to use. [%csl Gb6,Rb7][%cal Gb4b5] } (22. h3 { Fine, but a5 was ready now. } 22... Ne4 23. Bd3 Bf6 { His knight reached e4 first. Still better. }) (22. Qd4 { The queen comes to d4 first. Also fine. } 22... Qd8 23. a5 Qf8 { The pawn lands on a5 one move later, and you keep your edge. }) (22. Bd3 { The bishop moves first. Also fine. } 22... Qd8 23. a5 g6 { The same squares, one move later, and you are clearly better. }) (22. b5 { The break, a move too soon. } 22... Rxc5 23. Rxc5 Rxc5 24. bxa6 bxa6 { The c pawn is gone, and you are only slightly better. [%csl Rc5] }) 1-0


[Event "Strategy: the weak colour, remove the guard"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Role "exercise"]
